\subsubsection{Effect of Different LLMs}
\label{sssec:ablation_llm}
According to Table~\ref{table:st_enx} and \ref{table:mt_enx_wmt}, LLaMA-2 has shown excellent multilingual ability.
To further investigate the role of this ability in GenTranslate, we select two latest multilingual LLMs for comparison, \emph{i.e.}, BigTranslate and ALMA-13b.
Table~\ref{table:ablation_llm} shows that both of them perform worse than LLaMA-2-13b for ST and MT tasks.
One explanation is, BigTranslate and ALMA-13b are finetuned on MT task that requires cross-lingual ability, while the En$\rightarrow$X GenTranslate mainly requires strong monolingual ability of language X, such mismatch may explain why MT finetuning fails to enhance GenTranslate. 
