\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
In this paper, we propose a generative paradigm for translation tasks, namely GenTranslate, which leverages LLMs to integrate the diverse candidates in the decoded $N$-best list and generate a higher-quality translation result.
Furthermore, we release a HypoTranslate dataset to support LLM finetuning, which contains over $592$K hypotheses-translation pairs in 11 languages.
Experimental evidence on various speech and machine translation benchmarks shows that our GenTranslate significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art model.

